   "subject": "Re: R crashes with secr when using detection covariates",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve never seen an error like that. You seem to be making a big analysis out of a small dataset (100 detections). Why 25k pixels? First I suggest reducing your detection (trap? time? animal?) covariates to 2-3 levels, and trying just one covariate at a time. &#39;secr&#39; doesn&#39;t cope well with trap covariates, nor with any detection covariate that has many distinct values. Possibly you have measured something on a continuous scale at each of the 600 camera locations? If that works at all it will be very very slow to fit, for no real gain in insight.<br>Murray</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Monday, April 30, 2018 at 3:29:20 PM UTC+12, Koustubh Sharma wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" lang=\"EN-US\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:navy\">Dear all,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:navy\">We have been running models on a camera trapping dataset with nearly 600 cameras (but less than 100 captures) using secr. The mask has nearly 25k pixels. While the models work ok when using density covariates, R crashes when I use any detection covariates, irrespective of whether I parameterize lambda0 or sigma.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:navy\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:navy\">I have tried to use my personal PC as well as a 32 core system with 256GB memory, but face the same issue.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none\"><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:navy\"> </span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:navy\">Below is the command, along with the last lines that show up on the Console before it crashes:</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:navy\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:8.0pt;font-family:&quot;